'''The Matter of Using Toydarian Territory to Aid the Shipment of Relief Supplies to the Citizens of Ryloth''' was a diplomatic contention initiated when [[Senator/Legends|Senator]] [[Bail Prestor Organa/Legends|Bail Organa]] and [[Junior Representative/Legends|Representative]] [[Jar Jar Binks/Legends|Jar Jar Binks]] attempted to persuade [[King/Legends|King]] [[Katuunko/Legends|Katuunko]] and his [[Minister]]s to allow [[Toydaria/Legends|Toydaria]] to be used as a staging ground for sending aid to the starving troops and [[Twi'lek/Legends|Twi'lek]] civilians on [[Ryloth/Legends|Ryloth]]. The [[Confederacy of Independent Systems/Legends|Confederacy of Independent Systems]] intervened on the matter of their neutrality, sending [[Senator/Legends|Senator]] [[Lott Dod/Legends|Lott Dod]] of the [[Trade Federation/Legends|Trade Federation]] to persuade the [[Toydarian/Legends|Toydarian]] government to stay out of the war. After much debate, King Katuunko decided to send supplies to Ryloth, as long as the Separatists did not find out. The supplies reached the [[Battle of Ryloth/Legends|battle]]-torn planet successfully, and caused Katuunko to reconsider Toydaria's position in the war.

==Prelude==
[[File:Battle_of_Ryloth_SL.png|thumb|left|210px|Republic and Separatist forces battle on Ryloth.]]
On the [[Outer Rim Territories/Legends|Outer Rim Territories]] world of [[Ryloth/Legends|Ryloth]], the [[Grand Army of the Republic/Legends|forces]] of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems/Legends|Confederacy of Independent Systems]] was locked in combat against the [[Galactic Republic/Legends|Galactic Republic]] to stop the droid invasion of the [[Twi'lek/Legends|Twi'lek's]] world. [[Jedi/Legends|Jedi]] [[Jedi Master/Legends|Master]] [[Ima-Gun Di/Legends|Ima-Gun Di]] and [[Clone Captain/Legends|Captain]] [[Keeli/Legends|Keeli]] led a campaign on the surface, allied with the [[Twi'lek freedom fighters/Legends|Twi'lek freedom fighters]] lead by [[General/Legends|General]] [[Cham Syndulla/Legends|Cham Syndulla]]. Up in space, [[Admiral/Legends|Admiral]] [[Dao/Legends|Dao]] lead the [[Republic Navy/Legends|Republic Navy]] against the Separatist fleet. However, both Dao and General Di ran out of food, medical supplies, and ammunition after fighting without any reinforcements. Dao's ships were all destroyed, but were fortunate enough to contact the [[Jedi High Council/Legends|Jedi High Council]] on [[Coruscant/Legends|Coruscant]] to send word of assistance. [[Grand Master/Legends|Grand Master]] [[Yoda/Legends|Yoda]] and Masters [[Mace Windu/Legends|Mace Windu]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi/Legends|Obi-Wan Kenobi]] received the message, and in response asked [[Alderaanian/Legends|Alderaanian]] [[Senator/Legends|Senator]] [[Bail Prestor Organa/Legends|Bail Prestor Organa]], who had just ran a successful supply mission on the [[Tantive IV/Legends|''Tantive IV'']] to [[Toydaria/Legends|Toydaria]] to negotiate a supply base with their government. The Jedi also sent [[Gungan/Legends|Gungan]] [[Junior Representative/Legends|Representative]] [[Jar Jar Binks/Legends|Jar Jar Binks]] to assist Organa. However, the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems/Legends|Confederacy of Independent Systems]] intercepted details of the plans and [[Count/Legends|Count]] [[Dooku/Legends|Dooku]] dispatched [[Trade Federation/Legends|Trade Federation]] [[Senator/Legends|Senator]] [[Lott Dod/Legends|Lott Dod]] to prevent any deal from being taken place.

==The debate==
After arriving on Toydaria, Organa and Binks faced the [[Toydarian royal guard]], who denied them to leave the area as they were "off-worlders". Despite this, the Senator's were able to speak with the King and his minsters. However, shortly after their arrival, Lott Dod intervened in the negotiations right when Katuunko and the ministers were convinced to aid Ryloth. Dod pointed out that they would not be aiding civilians but soldiers, which went against there neutrality and such an action would anger the [[Separatist Senate/Legends|Separatist Parliament]] and cause damage to the Trade Federation which would mean they would have to pull out of important contracts with [[Toydaria/Legends|Toydaria]].

Although the request for aid was denied Katuunko decided that he would allow Bail Organa to send what supplies they had with them to Ryloth so long as the Federation was not to find out. However, the king unofficially expressed his interests in having his planet join the [[Galactic Republic/Legends|Galactic Republic]] to the Republic diplomats.

==Aftermath==
Organa and Binks would tell the news of Toydaria's reconsideration to the [[Jedi Council/Legends|Jedi Council]], who later sent [[Jedi Master/Legends|Jedi Master]] [[Yoda/Legends|Yoda]] to [[Battle of Rugosa/Legends|negotiate]] with Katuunko. The supplies sent to Ryloth breached the blockade of the planet, saving the citizens' lives before starvation and low medically supplies could kill off most, despite Jedi Master Di's death. This would allow the Republic to start planning their liberation of the planet, which almost failed.

